---
import InstallPage from "../../../../layouts/InstallPage.astro";
import InstallTrouble from "../../../../components/ui/InstallTrouble.astro";
import SniffiesBookmarkletCode from "../../../../components/ui/SniffiesBookmarkletCode.astro";
---

<InstallPage
  header="Bookmarklet (iOS)"
  description="Install the Sniffies Tools bookmarklet on iPhone browsers."
>
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <strong>⚠️ Warning: this is the worst experience of the three installs.</strong>
      A bookmarklet can't install itself like an extension or userscript can. You
      have to set it up by hand, and then run it manually every time you open or
      refresh sniffies.com. It also has the fewest features. If you can use the
      Chrome extension or a userscript instead, do that.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    For Chrome, Firefox, Edge, or any other non-Safari browser on iPhone. Every
    iOS browser is required to use Safari's engine under the hood, so Safari's <strong
      >Userscripts</strong
    > app and extensions like Tampermonkey aren't available outside Safari itself.
    A bookmarklet is the fallback: a bookmark that runs a bit of code on the page
    you're on instead of opening a link. It works in Safari too, with no app to install.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Heads up:</strong> the bookmarklet supports opening profiles outside
    your free radius and raising the selection caps on Sniffies' Sexuality, Body Type
    and Position filters. It can't spoof your location, block bots, or add the Gender,
    Height, Weight and Last Online filters, because a bookmarklet only runs after
    the page has already loaded. For those, switch to Safari and use
    the{" "}
    <a href="/projects/sniffies-project/install/userscript-ios/">
      Userscripts app install
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h2>Step 1: Copy the Bookmarklet Code</h2>
  <SniffiesBookmarkletCode />

  <!-- TODO screenshot: Step 1. The copy button / copied confirmation for the bookmarklet code. -->

  <h2>Step 2: Bookmark a Page</h2>
  <p>
    iOS browsers won't let you save the code as a bookmark directly, so bookmark
    any page first (this one works):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Safari:</strong> tap the Share button, then{" "}
      <strong>Add Bookmark</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Chrome:</strong> tap <strong>⋯</strong>, then{" "}
      <strong>Add to Bookmarks</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <!-- TODO GIF (screen recording on the phone, ~15s): Step 2, adding the bookmark (iOS). Show where the share/menu button is, since it is the hardest part to describe in words. -->

  <h2>Step 3: Turn the Bookmark into the Bookmarklet</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open your bookmarks and tap <strong>Edit</strong>, then tap the bookmark
      you just added
    </li>
    <li>Rename it to "Sniffies Tools"</li>
    <li>
      Delete everything in its address/URL field and paste the code from Step 1
    </li>
    <li>Save</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- TODO GIF (screen recording on the phone, ~15s): Step 3. Record: open the bookmarks list, edit the bookmark, rename it, paste the code into the URL field, save. Highlight that the URL field must be fully cleared first. -->

  <h2>Using It</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open sniffies.com and wait for the map to load</li>
    <li>
      Run the bookmarklet:
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Safari:</strong> open your bookmarks and tap "Sniffies Tools"
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Chrome and others:</strong> tap the address bar, type "Sniffies
          Tools", and tap the bookmark in the suggestions. Opening it from the bookmarks
          list may not run it on the current page.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      You'll see a "Sniffies Tools loaded!" message, and a Sniffies Tools button
      will appear in the map's row of icons
    </li>
    <li>
      Tap that button, open{" "}
      <strong>Open Profiles Outside Boundary</strong>, and tap{" "}
      <strong>Enable</strong>. Set <strong>Open in</strong> to{" "}
      <strong>New tab</strong> — opening in the current tab reloads the page, which
      unloads the bookmarklet.
    </li>
    <li>
      To raise the selection caps, open <strong>Profile Filters</strong>, tap{" "}
      <strong>Enable</strong>, then open the Cruisers section of Sniffies' Map
      Layers menu.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    The bookmarklet only lasts until the page reloads, so run it again each time
    you open or refresh sniffies.com.
  </p>

  <!-- TODO GIF (screen recording on the phone, ~15s): Using it. Record: open sniffies.com, wait for the map, tap the Sniffies Tools bookmark from the address bar, and show the panel opening. This is the step people get stuck on. -->

  <h2>Updating</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing to do. The bookmark loads the latest version every time you run it.
  </p>

  <p>
    If your browser doesn't let you edit a bookmark's URL, or the bookmarklet
    doesn't run, let me know which browser below and I'll add specific steps.
  </p>
  <InstallTrouble />
</InstallPage>
